    "https://careers.jsu.edu/jobs/speech-language-pathology-clinical-director-instructor-jacksonville-al-main-campus-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Speech Language Pathology Clinical Director/Instructor",
      "description": "Speech Language Pathology Clinical Director/Instructor - Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Back to JSU My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Speech Language Pathology Clinical Director/Instructor Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States, 36265 Faculty 12-Month (annual leave accruing) Jacksonville State University Clinical Director & Instructor, Speech-Language Pathology Jacksonville State University seeks a dynamic and experienced Speech-Language Pathologist for a 12-month, instructor position as Clinical Director. This faculty appointment requires a leader who will design, implement, and oversee all clinical education components of the speech language pathology programs, in addition to holding a full faculty role with teaching, and service responsibilities, ensuring students receive high-quality clinical training that meets Council on Academic Accreditation in Audiology and Speech-Language Pathology (CAA) standards. The Clinical Director works in close partnership with the Program Director to build a program grounded in clinical excellence, ethical practice, and strong community partnerships. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Clinical Education Leadership Design, implement, and continuously evaluate the clinical education curriculum in accordance with CAA standards and ASHA certification requirements Identify, establish, and maintain external practicum and clinical placement sites throughout the region Negotiate and manage affiliation agreements and contracts with clinical partner sites Ensure compliance with all federal, state, and accreditation regulations governing clinical practice and supervision (e.g., HIPAA, FERPA, ASHA Standards) Serve as a liaison between the university and clinical education partners, including hospitals, schools, private practices, and rehabilitation facilities Clinical Supervision and Student Development Provide direct clinical supervision to students in on-campus and/or off-campus clinical settings Recruit, train, and evaluate off-site clinical supervisors and preceptors Monitor student clinical competency development and progress toward ASHA certification standards Track and document student clinical hours, ensuring compliance with CAA and ASHA requirements Address student remediation needs related to clinical performance in coordination with program faculty Maintain clinical education records and documentation systems for accreditation reporting Program Development and Administration Collaborate with the Program Director on strategic planning, curriculum integration, and accreditation self-study preparation Establish policies and procedures for clinical practicum, including student clinical handbooks and site agreements Participate in program assessment and continuous improvement processes related to clinical outcomes Prepare clinical education reports required for CAA accreditation and other regulatory bodies Faculty Responsibilities Teach courses in speech-language pathology, including clinical methods and practicum courses Participate in professional service Maintain professional development and continuing education requirements, including clinical certification renewal Required Qualifications Education and Licensure Master's degree in Speech-Language Pathology from a CAA-accredited program Current state licensure in Speech-Language Pathology (Alabama licensure required within one year of appointment) Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology (CCC-SLP) from ASHA Eligibility to hold a Clinical Supervisor designation in accordance with ASHA standards At least 3 years of experience as a Clinical Director, Clinical Coordinator, or Director of Clinical Education in a CSD program Experience Demonstrated experience supervising graduate clinicians in clinical or practicum settings Experience with clinical program administration, site development, or clinical education coordination Familiarity with CAA accreditation standards related to clinical education Professional Competencies Comprehensive knowledge of CAA accreditation standards and ASHA certification requirements as they pertain to clinical education Strong understanding of evidence-based clinical practice across the lifespan and diverse disorder areas Demonstrated leadership, organizational, and relationship-building skills Excellent written and verbal communication abilities Proficiency in clinical documentation systems and data management for accreditation purposes Ability to build and sustain community and clinical partnerships Preferred Qualifications Direct experience with CAA accreditation site visits and self-study processes related to clinical education Experience launching or restructuring a clinical education program Knowledge of telepractice and technology-based service delivery models Active professional involvement in ASHA or other relevant professional organizations Experience developing interprofessional clinical education opportunities This 12-month faculty position has an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. Application Requirements Applicants must submit the following materials to be considered for the position: Cover letter addressing clinical leadership experience and vision for clinical education Current curriculum vitae Contact information for three professional references About Jacksonville, Alabama Jacksonville offers an exceptional quality of life in the heart of Alabama's scenic Appalachian foothills. Located strategically between Birmingham and Atlanta, residents enjoy easy access to major metropolitan areas while embracing the charm of a vibrant college town. The area boasts beautiful natural landscapes with numerous parks, hiking trails, and outdoor recreation opportunities at nearby Cheaha State Park and Talladega National Forest. Jacksonville features a thriving downtown district with local restaurants, shops, and cultural venues, complemented by excellent schools and family-friendly neighborhoods. The cost of living is remarkably affordable compared to major metropolitan areas, allowing for a comfortable lifestyle with access to quality healthcare, recreational facilities, and a strong sense of community. The region's rich history, combined with Jacksonville State University's cultural and athletic events, creates a dynamic environment that attracts professionals seeking both career growth and an outstanding work-life balance. About Jacksonville State University Founded in 1883, Jacksonville State University, also known as Jax State, is a learning-centered comprehensive public university in Jacksonville, Alabama. Nestled in the Appalachian foothills of northeast Alabama, midway between Birmingham and Atlanta, Jax State is home to more than 10,000 students from more than 60 countries. As a learning-centered university, it strives to challenge students academically in a responsive environment and supports them in achieving their educational, career and personal goals. As an institution of higher learning, it seeks to produce broadly educated graduates prepared for global engagement while promoting scholarly research and service activities that align with its academic and professional strengths. Jax State is recognized as a top-tier regional university, climbing steadily in the U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges Rankings over the past four years. Also known as “the friendliest campus in the South,” Jax State offers a diverse and comprehensive range of academic programs designed to prepare students for successful careers and lifelong learning. The University provides 46 undergraduate degree programs, 12 undergraduate microcredentials and certificates, 64 master's programs, three doctoral programs, seven Educational Specialist (EdS) programs and 15 graduate certificate programs and microcredentials. Many of these programs are available entirely online, offering flexibility to accommodate students' schedules and learning preferences. The University maintains a student-to-faculty ratio of 18:1, ensuring personalized instruction and mentorship in a supportive learning environment. With one of the highest percentages of accredited programs among universities nationwide, Jax State is committed to academic excellence and student success. For more information, visit www.jsu.edu . Clery Notice: In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act, https://www.clerycenter.org/the-clery-act the Jacksonville State University Police provide information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three calendar years. The JSU Annual Campus Security and Fire Report is available online at: https://www.jsu.edu/police/docs/cleryannualreport.pdf Equal Employment Opportunity: Jax State is an Equal Employment and Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Recommended Jobs Adjunct Faculty - Family & Consumer Sciences (Fall 2026 - Spring 2027) Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Education and Professional Studies The Department of Family and Consumer Sciences is seeking adjunct faculty members to teach courses in the program areas of Child Development, Child Life Studies, Human Sciences, Hospitality and Culinary Management, Merchandising, FCS Education, and Career Technical Education at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. These courses are offered in-person, hybrid, and online with experience in all three instruction methods preferred. Maintenance Supervisor Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Finance & Admin The Supervisor, Maintenance oversees those employees in the building trades skills such as carpenters, electricians, plumbers, painters, locksmiths and movers.  Collaboratively, the Supervisor and his crews maintain, refurbish, and repair all University facilities so that they are sound, comfortable, and aesthetically appealing. Assistant Professor, Emergency Management and Public Administration Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Social and Behavioral Sciences This position will be responsible for teaching graduate and undergraduate courses in both emergency management and public administration programs. The candidate will contribute to teaching the core curriculum of the MPA program, in particular courses in the areas of Organizational Studies, Public Personnel Management, and Nonprofit Management. The candidate should also be able to teach emergency management courses at the graduate level, including research methods and guide emergency management doctoral students in their dissertation research. The candidate must be committed to teaching in different modalities, especially in an online format. Jax State offers the most comprehensive emergency management programs in the nation, from bachelor’s to doctorate levels. JSU's NASPAA-accredited MPA program is also unique in that it offers concentrations in political science, emergency management, criminal justice, GIS, and administrative management. 700 Pelham Rd N Jacksonville, AL 36265 Phone: 1-800-231-5291 or 1-256-782-5781 Email: info@jsu.edu Facebook Youtube Instagram © 2026 Jacksonville State University Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
