    "https://careers.jsu.edu/jobs/instructor-communication-jacksonville-al-main-campus-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Instructor Communication",
      "description": "Instructor Communication - Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Back to JSU My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Instructor Communication Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States, 36265 Faculty 9-Month Jacksonville State University Instructor, Communication The Department of Communication invites applications for the position of Instructor in Communication, specializing in broadcast production and broadcast journalism. This non-tenure track position carries a 4/4 teaching load and 9 months of full-time service. The program is industry-focused and student-centered. We are looking for someone who has spent significant time in the field telling stories across platforms (broadcast newsrooms, multimedia production houses, digital news startups, or sports media operations) and wants to bring that expertise into the classroom. We balance hands-on skills with an integrated approach to broadcast production in journalism and other forms of content creation. Special consideration will be given to those who can teach creative and experiential courses in broadcast news and media production. The ideal candidate will maintain professional currency and collaborate with program faculty to ensure alignment between professional practice and academic foundations. This position requires the following qualifications: All applicants must have a master’s degree in mass communication, journalism, media production or a related field 3-5 years of industry experience in broadcast journalism, journalism, multimedia production, media operations and/or news production. The department will give priority to applicants who have: Evidence of quality prior teaching at the undergraduate level. Philosophical commitment to digital, technological, and disciplinary integration. Background to bridge our digital journalism and digital media production curricula and help students develop industry-ready skills. The position has an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. The Department of Communication earned full accreditation from the Accrediting Council for Education in Journalism and Mass Communication in April of 2023. We strive to offer a high-impact, industry-current approach to teaching. Our approach helps builds a strong reputation for producing job-ready graduates who are well-rounded citizens. Courses are offered through various delivery formats including face-to-face, hybrid/blended, and 100% on-line. JSU also serves a robust population of nontraditional and first-generation learners. Quality teaching will be the successful candidate’s primary responsibility balanced with creative production aligned with the position, as well as service to the department supporting our student media and contributing to the ongoing development and innovation in our curriculum. About Jax State Located in the Appalachian foothills of northeast Alabama, midway between Birmingham and Atlanta, Jax State is home to more than 10,400 students representing 63 countries. As a learning-centered university, it strives to challenge students academically in a responsive environment, meeting their educational, career and personal goals. As an academic institution, it seeks to produce broadly educated graduates prepared for global engagement. As a public, comprehensive university, it promotes excellence in scholarly and service activities consistent with its academic and professional strengths. For a complete list of Goals, Core Values and Strategies to fulfill this Mission, go to the JSU Strategic Plan home page. Academically Jax State offers 113 academic programs and concentrations, including bachelor's, master's, post-baccalaureate, doctoral and advanced certificate programs in a variety of disciplines that prepare graduates for meaningful careers and ongoing education.  More than 40 online programs are offered.  The University features six colleges on its 459-acre campus – Arts, Humanities and Sciences; Business and Industry; Education and Professional Studies; Health Professions and Wellness; Social and Behavioral Sciences; and Library. Most academic programs have discipline-specific accreditations, a reflection of their quality and JSU’s commitment to excellence. Clery Notice: In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act, https://www.clerycenter.org/the-clery-act the Jacksonville State University Police provide information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three calendar years. The JSU Annual Campus Security and Fire Report is available online at: https://www.jsu.edu/police/docs/cleryannualreport.pdf Equal Employment Opportunity: Jax State is an Equal Employment and Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 5d3001db Last Name (required) cda689b9 Email (required) 71109779 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Adjunct Faculty - Family & Consumer Sciences (Fall 2026 - Spring 2027) Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Education and Professional Studies The Department of Family and Consumer Sciences is seeking adjunct faculty members to teach courses in the program areas of Child Development, Child Life Studies, Human Sciences, Hospitality and Culinary Management, Merchandising, FCS Education, and Career Technical Education at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. These courses are offered in-person, hybrid, and online with experience in all three instruction methods preferred. Maintenance Supervisor Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Finance & Admin The Supervisor, Maintenance oversees those employees in the building trades skills such as carpenters, electricians, plumbers, painters, locksmiths and movers.  Collaboratively, the Supervisor and his crews maintain, refurbish, and repair all University facilities so that they are sound, comfortable, and aesthetically appealing. Assistant Professor, Emergency Management and Public Administration Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Social and Behavioral Sciences This position will be responsible for teaching graduate and undergraduate courses in both emergency management and public administration programs. The candidate will contribute to teaching the core curriculum of the MPA program, in particular courses in the areas of Organizational Studies, Public Personnel Management, and Nonprofit Management. The candidate should also be able to teach emergency management courses at the graduate level, including research methods and guide emergency management doctoral students in their dissertation research. The candidate must be committed to teaching in different modalities, especially in an online format. Jax State offers the most comprehensive emergency management programs in the nation, from bachelor’s to doctorate levels. JSU's NASPAA-accredited MPA program is also unique in that it offers concentrations in political science, emergency management, criminal justice, GIS, and administrative management. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 9d51faf2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Faculty 9-Month Faculty 9-Month Locations Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States First Name (required) 42071988 Last Name (required) 8bdb346b Email (required) 6c854e69 Send Please wait... Done No