    "https://careers.jsu.edu/jobs/professor-of-art-design-illustration-jacksonville-al-main-campus-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Professor of Art & Design, Illustration",
      "description": "Professor of Art & Design, Illustration - Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States Back to JSU My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Professor of Art & Design, Illustration Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama, United States, 36265 Faculty 9-Month Jacksonville State University Professor of Art, Illustration Named Alabama's #1 employer for 2025 by Forbes Magazine! Read more here ! Jacksonville State University is seeking applicants for a tenure-track position in Illustration at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. The selected candidate will be expected to teach a 3/3 load and fully engage in departmental duties, committee work, campus activities, and scholarship/creative activity. The Department of Art + Design at Jacksonville State University is accredited by NASAD and offers an MFA in Visual Communication Design and a BFA degree in Studio Art with concentrations in Ceramics, Illustration, Graphic Design, Painting, Photography, and Printmaking. The department also offers a BA in Art History and Art Minors in Studio Art, Photography, and Art History. The department has a highly collegial faculty and supportive administration, with highly favorable student-teacher ratios, well equipped studio spaces with budget allotments for new technologies, and a diverse student population. The Illustration concentration is a growing degree program seeking a new faculty member to make significant contributions in vision, teaching, curriculum planning, and research. This faculty member will be primarily responsible for courses in the Illustration concentration, but should be prepared to teach at all levels, from Art Foundations to graduate-level courses. Physical Requirements: Teaching requires time with students in the studio and labs. Candidates should be able to prepare and present assignments and evaluate students’ work in progress. A successful candidate should be available for mentoring students during office hours and as needed. Candidates should be able to move between art buildings and administrative buildings on campus for meetings. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Successful candidates must demonstrate a broad understanding of contemporary illustration practice and theory, as well as proficiency with both traditional illustration media and current industry-standard software. Their work should demonstrate mastery of formal design principles and conceptual underpinning. The successful candidate will also demonstrate excellence in teaching through a high-quality student work portfolio. Minimum Qualifications: This position requires an MFA or MDes from a regionally accredited institution in Illustration, Animation, Studio Art, Visual Communication, or related field. Proficiency in the use of industry standard software is required. This includes but is not limited to the current Adobe Creative Suite, as well as other software related to area(s) of expertise. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates with one or more of the following qualifications: Two or more years teaching at the university level beyond a teaching assistantship. Extensive experience in the field of professional illustration with a diverse client base. Additional areas of expertise beyond illustration, including but not limited to animation and other time-based media, graphic design, new media, 3-D modeling, painting, and drawing. Demonstrated excellence in curriculum development. A robust exhibition record and/or evidence of scholarly research in the form of conference presentations and publications. Instructions to Applicants: To demonstrate a record of professional and creative accomplishment, creative work samples are required to be submitted in a digital portfolio. Submission of 20 samples of creative work in pdf or URL format, and 20 samples of students' work in pdf or URL format are required. Send pdf or URL to bmiles@jsu.edu . If samples of student work are unavailable, please explain in the cover letter. Application must be made on-line with a curriculum vita, research statement, teaching philosophy, cover letter, and unofficial copies of all earned transcripts. Review of applications will begin November 16, 2026, with on-campus interviews beginning in January 2027. The position has an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. About Jax State Located in the Appalachian foothills of northeast Alabama, midway between Birmingham and Atlanta, Jax State is home to more than 10,400 students representing 63 countries. As a learning-centered university, it strives to challenge students academically in a responsive environment, meeting their educational, career and personal goals. As an academic institution, it seeks to produce broadly educated graduates prepared for global engagement. As a public, comprehensive university, it promotes excellence in scholarly and service activities consistent with its academic and professional strengths. For a complete list of Goals, Core Values and Strategies to fulfill this Mission, go to the JSU Strategic Plan home page. Academically Jax State offers 113 academic programs and concentrations, including bachelor's, master's, post-baccalaureate, doctoral and advanced certificate programs in a variety of disciplines that prepare graduates for meaningful careers and ongoing education.  More than 40 online programs are offered.  The University features six colleges on its 459-acre campus – Arts, Humanities and Sciences; Business and Industry; Education and Professional Studies; Health Professions and Wellness; Social and Behavioral Sciences; and Library. Most academic programs have discipline-specific accreditations, a reflection of their quality and JSU’s commitment to excellence. Clery Notice: In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act, https://www.clerycenter.org/the-clery-act the Jacksonville State University Police provide information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three calendar years. The JSU Annual Campus Security and Fire Report is available online at: https://www.jsu.edu/police/docs/cleryannualreport.pdf Equal Employment Opportunity: Jax State is an Equal Employment and Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Back to job listing Recommended Jobs Adjunct Faculty - Family & Consumer Sciences (Fall 2026 - Spring 2027) Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Education and Professional Studies The Department of Family and Consumer Sciences is seeking adjunct faculty members to teach courses in the program areas of Child Development, Child Life Studies, Human Sciences, Hospitality and Culinary Management, Merchandising, FCS Education, and Career Technical Education at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. These courses are offered in-person, hybrid, and online with experience in all three instruction methods preferred. Maintenance Supervisor Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama Not Applicable, Finance & Admin The Supervisor, Maintenance oversees those employees in the building trades skills such as carpenters, electricians, plumbers, painters, locksmiths and movers.  Collaboratively, the Supervisor and his crews maintain, refurbish, and repair all University facilities so that they are sound, comfortable, and aesthetically appealing. Assistant Professor, Emergency Management and Public Administration Jacksonville, AL (Main Campus), Alabama College of Social and Behavioral Sciences This position will be responsible for teaching graduate and undergraduate courses in both emergency management and public administration programs. The candidate will contribute to teaching the core curriculum of the MPA program, in particular courses in the areas of Organizational Studies, Public Personnel Management, and Nonprofit Management. The candidate should also be able to teach emergency management courses at the graduate level, including research methods and guide emergency management doctoral students in their dissertation research. The candidate must be committed to teaching in different modalities, especially in an online format. Jax State offers the most comprehensive emergency management programs in the nation, from bachelor’s to doctorate levels. JSU's NASPAA-accredited MPA program is also unique in that it offers concentrations in political science, emergency management, criminal justice, GIS, and administrative management. 700 Pelham Rd N Jacksonville, AL 36265 Phone: 1-800-231-5291 or 1-256-782-5781 Email: info@jsu.edu Facebook Youtube Instagram © 2026 Jacksonville State University Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
